link: Group-IB, the 0ktapus campaign | https://www.group-ib.com/blog/0ktapus/
link: MITRE ATT&CK T1111 | https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1111/
notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Cloudflare's post describes the mechanics of the phishing scam and how it was stopped. Twilio's is its incident report on employee and customer account compromise. Group-IB's post describes the 0ktapus campaign. The MITRE page defines T1111, Multi-Factor Authentication Interception, behind stage 02.

The background slides name their own sources: MITRE ATT&CK, the RFC that defines TOTP, OWASP and the csoh.org glossary.

